                <pb facs="0574" n="500" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg500"/>

                <head>No. 16.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[Telegram.–<date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1865-02-14">February 14</date>, at night.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">To the Consular Agent of the United States at
                        Ferrol:</hi></p>
                <p>Orders have been given not to allow the transshipment of men, munitions, and
                    supplies from the Louisa Ann Fanny to the Stonewall, and that she should not
                    better her condition in these respects while in Spanish waters. Watch over its
                    execution.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>PERRY,</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
